    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `initials` field on the Owner API response.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema (mirroring the existing `displayName` field), so the generated `OwnerDto` includes it.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping(target = \"initials\", ...)` on `toOwnerDto` plus a `toInitials(Owner)` default method that returns the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `\"john\"`/`\"smith\"` \u2192 `\"J.S.\"`).\n\nThis follows the existing `displayName` convention in the codebase (OpenAPI-generated DTO + MapStruct expression mapping), per the Spring conventions in CLAUDE.md. The `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesInitials` test and the full suite both pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
